  "published": "2026-08-26T07:10:00.76Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.64.0 hardens the trust paths and pays down latency. Auto-fixers can no longer corrupt project files: the transitive-conflict pin lands in exactly one unconditional, namespace-correct ItemGroup instead of every group in the file. --verify clears stale assets graphs before each capture, so a redirected build's leftover project.assets.json can no longer produce a false \"unchanged\" verdict; drift attribution considers every recorded decision and rejects contradictory ones. Rollback verifies SHA-256 integrity before restoring anything. Baselines report their own rot - stale entries and renamed rule IDs - across console, JSON and Markdown. --why accepts comma-separated package IDs (one scan, all answers, console or a new why-many JSON document under output schema 1.9.0), analysis output is byte-stable regardless of scan interleaving, and a grouped scan scheduler plus benchmarks/ harness guard the concurrency and cache wins with deterministic tests.",
